.TH false "" "Command"
.SH NAME
false \- unconditional failure
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfalse\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
false -- unconditional failure
Usage:	false
Does nothing and returns exit status 1.
.HE
.B false
does nothing and exits with a nonzero (failure) status.
It is useful in shell scripts to force a command to fail, and as the
never-satisfied condition of a loop, as in
.DS
.ta 8n
	\fBwhile false; do ... done\fR
.DE
which never executes its body.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B false
always exits with status 1.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sh ,
.B true
